findings.description:
`agreement_report` keys cells on `(level, template_name, model, template_content_hash)`. One `--template T --model M --level L` can therefore match several cells:
- an unversioned cell (hash `None`), which every existing store has;
- a pre-T1 hash cell;
- the current-hash cell;
- cells from earlier prompt edits.

T15 line 230 says "look up the pairing's current recommendation … filtered to this template/model/level" with no rule for picking one. A stale-hash cell at `GRADUATE` could be recorded as a graduation that is lapsed on arrival.

The task should select the cell whose hash equals the current template hash and refuse otherwise. That needs a public accessor: `_template_content_hash` is private, and pyright strict (`pyproject.toml:87`) rejects cross-module private use.
